module contract;

// Fluent Bit input-chunk name accessor — resource-projection vocabulary v1.
//
// Card PROD-CONTRACTS. One TRUSTED ASSUMPTION about one upstream function.
// It verifies nothing: the C body is not analyzed by this loader, and a
// declaration is a premise. A function-level `Safe` that rests on it is `Safe`
// RELATIVE TO this declaration, never a proof of the C implementation.
//
// ## The pinned body, read (`src/flb_input_chunk.c:3849` at Fluent Bit
// ## 66910c10a4d7eafa810b84229cf2dcf7b0f26f97)
//
//     flb_sds_t flb_input_chunk_get_name(struct flb_input_chunk *ic)
//     {
//         struct cio_chunk *ch;
//         ch = (struct cio_chunk *) ic->chunk;
//         return ch->name;
//     }
//
// `flb_sds_t` is `typedef char *flb_sds_t` (`include/fluent-bit/flb_sds.h:36`).
//
// ## Which mode is faithful
//
// The body reads two fields and returns. It allocates nothing, frees nothing,
// stores nothing and retains nothing, so the caller keeps exactly the
// obligations it had before the call: `resource_borrowed(ic)` states that, and
// it is the only v1 parameter mode with that caller-side effect (`owned`
// demands live custody, `consumed` transfers, `released` discharges, `out`
// creates custody at a destination, `stored` transfers under an owner and
// `removed` detaches from one).
//
// The RESULT is a pointer, and its faithful mode is nevertheless
// `resource_return_none()`, which reads "the call hands the caller no custody".
// `ch->name` is the chunk's OWN sds, allocated and freed by ChunkIO; the caller
// must not free it. Declaring `resource_return_owned(...)` here would install a
// cleanup obligation on the caller for storage another owner releases — a
// double-free the projection would then demand — so it is refused. That the
// mode is `None` rather than `Owned` is a decision about custody, not about the
// C type.
//
// ## What this declaration does NOT say — named, not hidden
//
// The returned pointer ALIASES INTO `ic` (it is `ic->chunk->name`), and this
// projection does not track the handback at all, so it does not model that
// alias and cannot notice a caller that outlives `ic` with it or frees it. Two
// separate things keep that from being a fail-open on this route, and both are
// stated as the bounded facts they are:
//
//   * the gateway admits a call whose result mode is `None` and whose
//     parameters are all `Borrowed` only where the result occupies a position
//     that needs no identity (card O04-TRACE's premises N6/N8) and never binds
//     it to a name, so it cannot outlive the statement; a body that STORED the
//     handback is a different statement shape and is refused;
//   * measured on the pinned corpus: all 20 call sites of this function in
//     `src/flb_input_chunk.c` — the only Fluent Bit unit in the 185-unit
//     corpus, and the only unit that calls it — occur inside a logging call's
//     argument list. NONE binds the result. The other two occurrences of the
//     name in the preprocessed unit are its prototype and its definition.
//
// That measurement is a fact about today's corpus, not a rule; the rule is the
// first bullet, and it is the gateway's, not this module's. The alias itself
// remains outside every claim here (O00 blockers B03/R13, and card O04-TRACE's
// `O04-TRACE-HANDBACK`).
//
// Card VERDICT-CONTRACT-PREMISE-ANNOTATIONS: stated on
// `flb_input_chunk_get_name` as `requires resource_premise(untracked_handback,
// "...")` (contract spec C04.18), so every verdict that rests on the
// declaration names it.
//
// This declaration also says nothing about `ic` being non-null — the body
// dereferences it unconditionally, but `resource_borrowed` imposes NO non-null
// precondition, which is the weaker statement and deliberately so: a mode that
// demanded entry custody would delete the caller's failure paths.
//
// ## A note on precedence
//
// This function is DEFINED in a corpus unit. A declared contract always wins
// over an inferred W4 summary, and a disagreement is reported as a
// `SummaryConflict` diagnostic rather than silently resolved either way. The
// unit's own definition stays analyzable and is not rewritten.

extern fn flb_input_chunk_get_name(ic: ptr<mut, u8>) -> ptr<mut, u8>
contract {
    requires resource_contract_v1;
    requires resource_premise(untracked_handback, "the result aliases into ic (it is ic->chunk->name) and this projection does not track it; resource_return_none is faithful only where the result is never bound or stored, which the gateway's admission of a call with a None result and only Borrowed parameters checks per site (card O04-TRACE premises N6 and N8); the alias itself is outside every claim here (O00 B03/R13, O04-TRACE-HANDBACK)");
    ensures normal resource_borrowed(ic);
    ensures normal resource_return_none();
};
